      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "spring jdbc ,let's understand how spring jdbc work and \nhow it's different from normal jdbc \n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "spring jdbc ,let's understand how spring jdbc work and \nhow it's different from normal jdbc \n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "3lYnaATs5dZ4LVwYJ1Fgd",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 514.8572387695312,
      "y": 322.8571472167969,
      "width": 836,
      "height": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bFm",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 348455252,
      "version": 382,
      "versionNonce": 863992684,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1763991036034,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "so in this module we will create a simple rest api with one \n/get route and one /post route ,we wont dive deep into how this route will \nwork our main focus will be how to create a service(buisness logic) and how \nit will comunicate with repository that is database logic communication",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "so in this module we will create a simple rest api with one \n/get route and one /post route ,we wont dive deep into how this route will \nwork our main focus will be how to create a service(buisness logic) and how \nit will comunicate with repository that is database logic communication",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "WCC2a4vLKLyD9U-S2j4x-",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 512.5712890625,
      "y": 452.1428527832031,
      "width": 907.4285888671874,
      "height": 450,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bFn",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 557194092,
      "version": 143,
      "versionNonce": 413878740,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1763991363420,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Spring JDBC is a module in Spring Framework which makes database access easier by\nusing JdbcTemplate.\n\nTraditional JDBC is verbose and requires you to manually:\n\n-Open connection\n\n-Create statements\n\n-Execute queries\n\n-Close ResultSet\n\n-Close Connection\n\n-Handle exceptions\n\nSpring JDBC removes all boilerplate using a template pattern.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Spring JDBC is a module in Spring Framework which makes database access easier by using JdbcTemplate.\n\nTraditional JDBC is verbose and requires you to manually:\n\n-Open connection\n\n-Create statements\n\n-Execute queries\n\n-Close ResultSet\n\n-Close Connection\n\n-Handle exceptions\n\nSpring JDBC removes all boilerplate using a template pattern.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "-h2CDqq5lspd4yRm3sOOf",
