      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1763993885760,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Now-lets understand hikariCP",
      "fontSize": 36,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Now-lets understand hikariCP",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "x7awwFzYa5sMF-VwlQ-o0",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 613.916920166711,
      "y": 11918.587525227287,
      "width": 922.9030923315269,
      "height": 325,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bGq",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1528174700,
      "version": 107,
      "versionNonce": 1979048148,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1763993913897,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "What is HikariCP?\n\nHikariCP is a high-performance JDBC connection pool used by Spring Boot as the\ndefault connection pool.\n\nThink of it like this:\n\n✅ Opening a DB connection is slow → 200–500 ms\n✅ HikariCP keeps connections ready → 0 ms\n❌ Normal JDBC → opens new connection every time (slow)\n✔ HikariCP → reuses existing connections (super–fast)\n\nIt is called the fastest JDBC connection pool in the Java ecosystem.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "What is HikariCP?\n\nHikariCP is a high-performance JDBC connection pool used by Spring Boot as the default connection pool.\n\nThink of it like this:\n\n✅ Opening a DB connection is slow → 200–500 ms\n✅ HikariCP keeps connections ready → 0 ms\n❌ Normal JDBC → opens new connection every time (slow)\n✔ HikariCP → reuses existing connections (super–fast)\n\nIt is called the fastest JDBC connection pool in the Java ecosystem.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "8Os1mtZAlmOodEfllYu4n",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 615.4556641742274,
      "y": 12281.488817132735,
      "width": 693,
      "height": 500,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bGr",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 5151596,
      "version": 40,
      "versionNonce": 1294852052,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1763993967154,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Why do we need a Connection Pool?\n\nBecause without pooling:\n\nEvery SQL = open connection → run SQL → close connection\n\n\nOpening DB connections is the slowest part of a JDBC operation.\n\nA connection pool:\n\na)Keeps a pool (bucket) of pre-opened DB connections\n\nb)When your code needs one → pool gives it instantly\n\nc)After work → connection is returned to pool\n\nd)NOT closed\n\nThis makes your application 10x faster and scalable.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Why do we need a Connection Pool?\n\nBecause without pooling:\n\nEvery SQL = open connection → run SQL → close connection\n\n\nOpening DB connections is the slowest part of a JDBC operation.\n\nA connection pool:\n\na)Keeps a pool (bucket) of pre-opened DB connections\n\nb)When your code needs one → pool gives it instantly\n\nc)After work → connection is returned to pool\n\nd)NOT closed\n\nThis makes your application 10x faster and scalable.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
