      "seed": 739973966,
      "version": 73,
      "versionNonce": 1689189138,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1763998196608,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "⭐ What is “In-memory Database”?\n\nH2 can run in memory:\n\nData is stored in RAM, not in a file.\n\n\nMeaning:\n\nWhen the Spring Boot app stops → database disappears\n\nPerfect for testing & learning\n\nVery fast\n\nSpring Boot default URL:\n\nspring.datasource.url=jdbc:h2:mem:testdb",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "⭐ What is “In-memory Database”?\n\nH2 can run in memory:\n\nData is stored in RAM, not in a file.\n\n\nMeaning:\n\nWhen the Spring Boot app stops → database disappears\n\nPerfect for testing & learning\n\nVery fast\n\nSpring Boot default URL:\n\nspring.datasource.url=jdbc:h2:mem:testdb",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
