      "seed": 994126770,
      "version": 46,
      "versionNonce": 1199514674,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1764004425368,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Let's understand what is a RowMapper",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Let's understand what is a RowMapper",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "0WvteiPibKm7VqUFCtlEf",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 655.0918629205383,
      "y": 32232.510899772187,
      "width": 748,
      "height": 425,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bIY",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 387271790,
      "version": 18,
      "versionNonce": 1000658738,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1764004536477,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "✅ What is a RowMapper in Spring JDBC?\n\nA RowMapper is an interface in Spring JDBC whose job is:\n\nTo convert a single row from the SQL ResultSet into a Java object.\n\nWhenever you run a query like:\n\njdbcTemplate.query(\"SELECT * FROM student\", new StudentRowMapper());\n\n\nSpring fetches all rows from the database.\n\nBut Spring does NOT know how to convert each row into your Student\nobject.\n\nSo Spring calls your RowMapper to do that conversion.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "✅ What is a RowMapper in Spring JDBC?\n\nA RowMapper is an interface in Spring JDBC whose job is:\n\nTo convert a single row from the SQL ResultSet into a Java object.\n\nWhenever you run a query like:\n\njdbcTemplate.query(\"SELECT * FROM student\", new StudentRowMapper());\n\n\nSpring fetches all rows from the database.\n\nBut Spring does NOT know how to convert each row into your Student object.\n\nSo Spring calls your RowMapper to do that conversion.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
