    {
      "id": "xrxeWQGYhgxmRnNsUf0xm",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 650.1119642571398,
      "y": 37099.70725505141,
      "width": 785.3997192382812,
      "height": 625,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bJ6",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1024804718,
      "version": 46,
      "versionNonce": 1566002482,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1764004845533,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "❗ RowMapper is NOT recursive\n\nIt never calls itself.\nSpring JDBC calls it once per row in the ResultSet.\n\nLet me explain clearly.\n\n✅ 1. How RowMapper Actually Works (Simple Explanation)\n\nSpring JDBC uses JdbcTemplate which internally does something like:\n\nwhile(resultSet.next()) {\n    call rowMapper.mapRow(resultSet, rowNumber)\n}\n\n\nSo the flow is:\n\nRow 1 → mapRow() called once  \nRow 2 → mapRow() called once  \nRow 3 → mapRow() called once  \n...\n\n\nThere is no recursive call, only a simple loop.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "❗ RowMapper is NOT recursive\n\nIt never calls itself.\nSpring JDBC calls it once per row in the ResultSet.\n\nLet me explain clearly.\n\n✅ 1. How RowMapper Actually Works (Simple Explanation)\n\nSpring JDBC uses JdbcTemplate which internally does something like:\n\nwhile(resultSet.next()) {\n    call rowMapper.mapRow(resultSet, rowNumber)\n}\n\n\nSo the flow is:\n\nRow 1 → mapRow() called once  \nRow 2 → mapRow() called once  \nRow 3 → mapRow() called once  \n...\n\n\nThere is no recursive call, only a simple loop.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
